      "note": "Uncommitted growing-dot triangular recursion rewrite. Because it reassociates the floating-point work, the sampled chain is NOT bitwise equal to the 2026-07-30 whole-vector baseline; per-trial PLL and n_eff both move. This is expected and is reported, not smoothed over."
    },
    "protocol": "Standard PPLBench, identical to the 2026-07-30 baseline: config standard/noisy_or_topic_matched_init, 4000 iterations, 1000 warmup, 4 trials as chains, model seed 12345, step_size 0.1, max_tree_depth 10, adapt_step_size true, adapt_mass_matrix true, dense inverse mass matrix via the harness dense-eye default (the config deliberately omits inverse_mass_matrix), cpu, 32 threads, CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES empty.",
    "replication": "Impulse: 3 clean replicates, each a complete 4-trial protocol run. NumPyro: 1 run under the identical protocol, for a contemporaneous reference wall. Headline wall is the MEDIAN of the replicate steady-state means; steady mean = mean of trials 1..3, dropping trial 0. Headline n_eff/s is the n_eff/s median of the replicate whose steady mean is the median. This is the same reduction used by nuts_allreal_impulse_rerun_2026-07-30.json and was verified to reproduce that file's numbers exactly before being applied here.",
    "machine": "192 cores, 503 GB, shared. Every replicate gated on 1-minute load average below 12 immediately before launch. Gate readings 4.52 / 4.74 / 4.46 for the three Impulse replicates and 3.87 for NumPyro. These are somewhat higher than the 2026-07-30 baseline's 3.89 / 2.12 / 2.75 because other users were active; all four passed the gate and no replicate overlapped another benchmark of ours.",
